337	    // A DECLINED REQUEST IS DISARMED IN THE SAME CONVERGENCE (PRINCIPLES.md).
338	    // Nothing else would: an issue left carrying `claude-queued` after its run was
339	    // refused is one no later scheduler run adopts and no person is told about, and one
340	    // whose mark — if re-applied — walks into the same refusal forever.
341	    // A LEGACY shadow item wrote its decline back to the issue it named. A marked
342	    // issue IS the item, so the decline's comment and its `rejected` status already
343	    // land where the person is looking and there is nothing to mirror (PRINCIPLES.md).
344	    if (fields.request && fields.request !== item.number) {
345	      await declineRequest(api, gh, repo, fields.request, item.number, plan.reason);
346	    }
347	    // A DECLINE IS A COMPLETED RUN, not a failure: the executor asked, got a
348	    // no, and closed the occurrence — so the record says `success` and the
349	    // reason sits beside it in the same comment.
350	    await close(api, gh, repo, item, STATUS_RUNNING_EXECUTOR, TASK_OBSOLETE, 'not_planned',
351	      `The precondition declined: ${plan.reason}`
352	      + (plan.standing
