1	// THE HARNESS — the fake world of `world/` wired to the real queue, and nothing
2	// else. It holds no model of the mechanism: every verdict a scenario asserts on
3	// was reached by the code under `src/`, driven here against an in-memory GitHub,
4	// a virtual clock and a scripted set of agent sessions.
5	//
6	// WHAT IT OWNS is a world and a cast:
7	//
8	//  - THE WORLD is `world/`: the clock and its event queue, the GitHub store, the
9	//    Actions ledger, the invocation endpoint, the agent sessions and the people.
10	//    Each of those modules says what it models and what it does not.
11	//  - THE CAST is the scenario's tasks. A scenario states a task the way a
12	//    declaration does — a cadence term, an `after`, whether it has a work step and
13	//    how long it takes — plus a `precondition` function standing for every
14	//    condition a real declaration would name in terms of its own signals. That
